//   to false, so the implication is vacuous. In the tight constrained branch,
//   ConstrainedStep returns either EOS (break) or a parser-valid next token;
//   AppendConstrainedToken therefore preserves parser validity. In the loose
//   symbol branch, ConstrainedSymbol returns symbolOut that is itself a valid
//   parser prefix, so assigning currentConstrainedOut := symbolOut preserves the
//   invariant.
